   `bg-gh-blue`, `text-gh-text-primary`, `bg-background`, and the rest -- and not one of the
   utilities they generated was ever used: every colour in this app is applied as an arbitrary
   value reading the `:root` custom property directly, `text-[var(--github-blue)]`. Tailwind emits
   only the utilities a file actually references, so the tokens never reached the stylesheet and
   removing them changes the generated CSS by zero bytes. What they cost was a reader's time, by
   presenting a second, parallel naming scheme for the same seven colours that nothing was written
   against. The `:root` block above stays as the single source for them. */
@theme inline {
  /* Typography is the visitor's system UI stack, matching GitHub's own. These two tokens are the
     only font definitions in the app: no web font is downloaded, so nothing here or in the build
     depends on an external font host. */

